# UI/Testing/QC Extraction Skill

Skill chuyên biệt để trích xuất specifications về UI, Testing, và Quality Control.

## Khi nào sử dụng

- Khi cần lấy UI/component specifications
- Khi cần trích xuất design system documentation
- Khi cần thu thập testing strategies và test cases
- Khi cần lấy QC/QA specifications và acceptance criteria

## UI Extraction Sections

### 1. Design System Documentation

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Color palettes và typography scales
- Spacing và grid systems
- Icon libraries
- Motion/animation specifications

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract color values
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=color], [style*=color]')).map(el => ({text: el.textContent, color: getComputedStyle(el).color}))"

# Extract spacing values
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=spacing], [style*=margin], [style*=padding]')).map(el => ({class: el.className, margin: getComputedStyle(el).margin, padding: getComputedStyle(el).padding}))"
```

### 2. Component Library

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Component types và variants
- Props/parameters
- State definitions
- Usage examples

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract component list
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=component], [class*=element]')).map(el => el.textContent)"

# Extract props tables
"$PWCLI" eval "JSON.stringify(Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('table')).map(t => ({name: t.previousElementSibling?.textContent, rows: Array.from(t.querySelectorAll('tr')).map(r => Array.from(r.children).map(c => c.textContent))})))"
```

### 3. Responsive Breakpoints

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Breakpoint definitions
- Device-specific layouts
- Mobile/tablet/desktop considerations

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract breakpoints
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre, code')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/breakpoint|media query|@media/)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

## Testing Extraction Sections

### 1. Test Strategy

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Testing pyramid/types
- Coverage requirements
- Tool recommendations
- CI/CD integration

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract testing approach
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('h1, h2, h3')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/test|spec/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"

# Extract tool names
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre code')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/jest|cypress|playwright|selenium|testing-library/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### 2. Test Cases

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Test case IDs và descriptions
- Preconditions
- Test steps
- Expected results
- Test data requirements

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract test cases structure
"$PWCLI" eval "JSON.stringify(Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('tr, li')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/test|TC-|step|given|when|then/i)).map(el => el.textContent))"

# Extract scenario outlines
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=scenario], [class*=test-case]')).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### 3. Mocking/Stubbing Guidelines

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Mock libraries
- Fixture strategies
- Data seeding
- API mocking

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract mocking patterns
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/mock|stub|spy|fake/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### 4. Performance Benchmarks

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Load time requirements
- Concurrent user limits
- Resource utilization
- SLA definitions

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract performance metrics
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('table, li')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/ms|second|concurrent|latency|throughput/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

## QC Extraction Sections

### 1. Acceptance Criteria

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Definition of Done
- Feature completion criteria
- Non-functional requirements
- Business rules validation

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract acceptance criteria
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=acceptance], [class*=criterion], [class*=done]')).map(el => el.textContent)"

# Extract requirements
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('h1, h2, h3')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/requirement|must|shall|should/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### 2. Bug Severity Levels

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Severity/criticality definitions
- Priority levels
- SLA for fixes
- Escalation paths

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract bug severity definitions
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=severity], [class*=priority], [class*=bug]')).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### 3. Release Criteria

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Release checklist
- Deployment gates
- Sign-off requirements
- Rollback procedures

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract release criteria
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=release], [class*=deploy], [class*=checklist]')).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### 4. Monitoring & SLA

**Tìm các thông tin:**
- Uptime requirements
- Error rate thresholds
- Response time SLAs
- Monitoring tools

**Extraction commands:**
```bash
# Extract SLA definitions
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('table, li')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/uptime|sla|99\.|availability/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

## Output Templates

### UI Specification Template

```markdown
# UI Specification - {Component/System}

## Overview
{Mô tả tổng quan về UI system}

## Design Tokens

### Colors
| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|-------|
| --primary | #007bff | Primary actions |
| --secondary | #6c757d | Secondary elements |

### Typography
| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|-------|
| --font-size-sm | 12px | Small text |
| --font-size-base | 14px | Body text |

### Spacing
| Token | Value |
|-------|-------|
| --spacing-xs | 4px |
| --spacing-sm | 8px |

## Components

### {ComponentName}
**Type:** {atomic|molecular|organismic}
**States:** {default, hover, active, disabled, error}

#### Props
| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| variant | string | 'default' | Visual variant |

#### Usage
\`\`\`jsx
<{ComponentName} variant="primary" />
\`\`\`
```

### Testing Template

```markdown
# Testing Specification - {Feature}

## Test Strategy

### Test Pyramid
- Unit Tests: {percentage}%
- Integration Tests: {percentage}%
- E2E Tests: {percentage}%

### Tools
- Test Runner: {tool}
- Assertions: {library}
- Mocking: {library}

## Test Cases

### TC-{id}: {Test Case Name}
**Priority:** {High|Medium|Low}
**Type:** {Positive|Negative|Boundary}

**Preconditions:**
1. {precondition 1}
2. {precondition 2}

**Test Steps:**
1. {step 1}
2. {step 2}

**Expected Results:**
{expected outcome}

## Test Data
\`\`\`json
{
  "testUser": { "email": "test@example.com" }
}
\`\`\`
```

### QC Template

```markdown
# QC Specification - {Feature/Module}

## Acceptance Criteria

### Functional
- [ ] {AC-1}
- [ ] {AC-2}

### Non-Functional
- [ ] {Performance requirement}
- [ ] {Security requirement}

## Bug Severity Definitions

| Severity | Definition | SLA |
|----------|------------|-----|
| Critical | System down | 4h |
| High | Major feature broken | 24h |
| Medium | Feature degraded | 1 week |
| Low | Minor issue | Next release |

## Release Checklist

- [ ] All acceptance criteria met
- [ ] Security review completed
- [ ] Performance benchmarks met
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] Sign-off obtained

## SLA Requirements

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Uptime | 99.9% |
| Response Time | < 200ms |
| Error Rate | < 0.1% |
```

## Navigation Pattern for UI/Testing/QC Pages

```bash
# 1. Open main documentation
"$PWCLI" open https://docs.example.com

# 2. Find UI/Testing/QC sections
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('nav a, [class*=sidebar] a')).map(a => ({text: a.textContent.trim(), href: a.getAttribute('href')}))"

# 3. Click through relevant sections
"$PWCLI" click e5  # UI/Guidelines
"$PWCLI" snapshot
"$PWCLI" screenshot

"$PWCLI" click e6  # Testing
"$PWCLI" snapshot
"$PWCLI" screenshot

"$PWCLI" click e7  # QC/Release
"$PWCLI" snapshot
"$PWCLI" screenshot
```

